## Core Context System

Read these documents before coding:
- project-context/prd.md - Requirements and goals
- project-context/architecture.md - System design and tech stack
- project-context/rules.md - Coding standards
- project-context/design.md - UI/UX guidelines
- project-context/tasks.md - Current work
- project-context/memory.md - Recent decisions

## Quality Standards

Apply these frameworks:
- Security: OWASP standards, input validation
- Privacy: GDPR, COPPA compliance
- Accessibility: WCAG 2.1 AA
- Performance: Core Web Vitals optimization
- SEO: Semantic HTML, meta tags

## Communication

Use token-efficient "caveman mode":
- Brief status updates
- No unnecessary verbosity
- Focus on implementation

## Behavior

1. Read context docs before changes
2. Follow established patterns
3. Update memory.md with decisions
4. Check quality frameworks
5. Use smart skill delegation when available

## Anti-Vibe-Coding

Do NOT:
- Use generic AI aesthetics
- Make arbitrary design choices
- Ignore existing design system
- Create fake data/testimonials
- Deviate from architecture without reason

Follow the systematic approach defined in project context.

